{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, PCA, single) achieved 0.485 acc / 0.464 F1, while config_016 (multimodal, PCA + ResNet50, concat, single) achieved 0.527 acc / 0.510 F1, a ~4.2% accuracy gain. However, we cannot yet decompose whether this gain comes from the image modality's independent predictive strength or from genuine cross-modal complementarity. Question: config_010 (image-only, single profile, ResNet50) establishes the image-only baseline using the exact same image encoder and profile setting as config_016, isolating the image modality's standalone contribution. Why this is the best next experiment: Without this baseline, we cannot calibrate how much of the multimodal gain is attributable to the image alone versus the fusion interaction, which is critical for deciding whether to invest further in fusion strategies, alternative encoders, or aggregation. It is a single-variable change (removing RNA) from config_016, making the comparison clean and informative. This foundational measurement will guide whether subsequent experiments should focus on improving fusion (config_017), adding multiprofile aggregation (config_018), or switching encoders."
}

